# Git — PRs for review, user merges

The user owns `main`. The agent never lands work there.

## Delivery order

1. Branch off current `main` (`feat/…` / `fix/…`). Do not commit on `main`.
2. One concern per branch/PR. Split unrelated requests (e.g. homepage vs error copy) into separate PRs. Stack later PRs on the earlier branch when they depend on it.
3. Commit locally (Conventional Commits, English). Push the branch. Open a PR to `main` (or the stacked base).
4. Required checks: `quality`, `api-test`, `web-e2e`. Fix the PR if CI is red. Do not merge.
5. Stop. Tell the user the PR URL. They review and merge.

## Never

- `git push` to `main` / `master`
- `gh pr merge`, merge-button equivalents, or “merge when green” loops
- Force-push to `main`

## After they merge

Do not fast-forward local `main` or restack later PRs unless they ask.

After `git pull` / branch switch: `npm run build:packages` (`dist/` is gitignored; stale types kill the API watch).
